---
import CodeBlock from './CodeBlock.astro';
import CopyButton from './CopyButton.astro';
import Section from './Section.astro';
import { authorUrl, cdn, repoUrl } from '../data';

const files = [
  { file: 'index.json', about: 'An array of all flags.', url: `${cdn}/index.json` },
  { file: 'by-code.json', about: 'An object of all flags, keyed by code.', url: `${cdn}/by-code.json` },
  { file: 'images/{CODE}.svg', about: 'One SVG image per flag, such as images/DE.svg.', url: `${cdn}/images/DE.svg` },
];

const indexExample = `[
  {
    "name": "Germany",
    "code": "DE",
    "emoji": "🇩🇪",
    "unicode": "U+1F1E9 U+1F1EA",
    "image": "${cdn}/images/DE.svg"
  }
]`;

const byCodeExample = `{
  "DE": {
    "name": "Germany",
    "emoji": "🇩🇪",
    "unicode": "U+1F1E9 U+1F1EA",
    "image": "${cdn}/images/DE.svg"
  }
}`;

const fields = [
  ['name', 'Germany', 'Name of the country or region, from Unicode CLDR.'],
  ['code', 'DE', 'ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code. See special codes for the exceptions.'],
  ['emoji', '🇩🇪', 'The flag emoji.'],
  ['unicode', 'U+1F1E9 U+1F1EA', 'Code points of the emoji, separated by spaces.'],
  ['image', '…/images/DE.svg', 'jsDelivr URL of the SVG image.'],
];

const specialCodes = [
  ['GB-ENG, GB-SCT, GB-WLS', 'England, Scotland and Wales. These are ISO 3166-2 subdivision codes.'],
  ['AC, CP, CQ, DG, EA, IC, TA', 'Ascension Island, Clipperton Island, Sark, Diego Garcia, Ceuta & Melilla, Canary Islands, Tristan da Cunha. ISO reserves these codes.'],
  ['EU, UN', 'European Union and United Nations. ISO reserves these codes.'],
  ['XK', 'Kosovo. A user-assigned code, used by the EU and others.'],
];

const polyfillInstall = 'npm install country-flag-emoji-polyfill';

const polyfillScript = `import { polyfillCountryFlagEmojis } from 'country-flag-emoji-polyfill';

polyfillCountryFlagEmojis();`;

const polyfillCss = `body {
  font-family: 'Twemoji Country Flags', system-ui, sans-serif;
}`;

const renamed = [
  ['England', 'ENGLAND', 'GB-ENG'],
  ['Scotland', 'SCOTLAND', 'GB-SCT'],
  ['Wales', 'WALES', 'GB-WLS'],
];

const link = 'text-link underline decoration-link/30 underline-offset-[3px] hover:decoration-link';
const inlineCode = 'rounded-sm bg-code px-1 py-px font-mono text-[0.86em]';
const th = 'border-b border-line py-2 pr-4 text-left text-[13px] font-medium text-muted';
const td = 'border-b border-line py-2.5 pr-4 align-top';
---

<Section id="files" title="Files">
  <p>
    Everything is in the <code class={inlineCode}>dist</code> folder of the package. The URLs below use jsDelivr. The same files are on <a class={link} href="https://unpkg.com/country-flag-emoji-json/">unpkg</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="relative overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class={th}>File</th>
          <th class={`${th} hidden sm:table-cell`}>Contents</th>
          <th class={`${th} pr-0 text-right`}><span class="sr-only">URL</span></th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          files.map((item, index) => (
            <tr>
              <td class={td}>
                <code class="whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-[13px] font-medium">{item.file}</code>
                <p class="mt-0.5 text-muted sm:hidden">{item.about}</p>
              </td>
              <td class={`${td} hidden text-muted sm:table-cell`}>{item.about}</td>
              <td class={`${td} py-1.5 pr-0 text-right`}>
                <span id={`file-url-${index}`} data-full={item.url} hidden></span>
                <CopyButton source={`#file-url-${index}`} label={`${item.file} URL`} text="Copy URL" />
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <CodeBlock id="example-index" code={indexExample} lang="json" title="index.json" />
  <CodeBlock id="example-by-code" code={byCodeExample} lang="json" title="by-code.json" />
</Section>

<Section id="fields" title="Fields">
  <p>Each flag has these fields. In <code class={inlineCode}>by-code.json</code>, the code is the key, so <code class={inlineCode}>code</code> is left out.</p>

  <div class="relative overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class={th}>Field</th>
          <th class={th}>Example</th>
          <th class={th}>Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          fields.map(([field, example, about]) => (
            <tr>
              <td class={`${td} font-mono text-[13px] font-medium`}>{field}</td>
              <td class={`${td} font-mono text-[13px] sm:whitespace-nowrap`}>{example}</td>
              <td class={`${td} text-muted`}>{about}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</Section>

<Section id="special-codes" title="Special codes">
  <p>Most codes are ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country codes. These ones are not.</p>

  <div class="relative overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class={th}>Code</th>
          <th class={th}>Flag</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          specialCodes.map(([codes, about]) => (
            <tr>
              <td class={`${td} font-mono text-[13px] font-medium sm:whitespace-nowrap`}>{codes}</td>
              <td class={`${td} text-muted`}>{about}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</Section>

<Section id="windows" title="Flags on Windows">
  <p>
    Windows has no flag emojis. It shows the two letters of the code instead, so the flag of Germany appears as <code class={inlineCode}>DE</code>. There are two fixes.
  </p>

  <ol class="space-y-4">
    <li class="flex gap-3">
      <span class="flex size-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line font-mono text-xs text-muted">1</span>
      <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
        <p class="font-medium">Use the SVG image</p>
        <p class="text-muted">Show the <code class={inlineCode}>image</code> URL in an <code class={inlineCode}>&lt;img&gt;</code> tag. It looks the same on every system. This is the most reliable fix.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="flex gap-3">
      <span class="flex size-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line font-mono text-xs text-muted">2</span>
      <div class="min-w-0 flex-1 space-y-3">
        <div>
          <p class="font-medium">Load a flag font</p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            <a class={link} href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/country-flag-emoji-polyfill">country-flag-emoji-polyfill</a> adds a flag font only when the browser needs it. Call it once, then put the font first in your CSS. This site does the same.
          </p>
        </div>
        <CodeBlock id="polyfill-install" code={polyfillInstall} lang="sh" title="Terminal" />
        <CodeBlock id="polyfill-script" code={polyfillScript} lang="js" title="JavaScript" />
        <CodeBlock id="polyfill-css" code={polyfillCss} lang="css" title="CSS" />
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
</Section>

<Section id="upgrading" title="Upgrading from v2">
  <p>There is one breaking change. England, Scotland and Wales now use ISO 3166-2 codes. Their old image files still exist, so old image URLs keep working.</p>

  <div class="relative overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class={th}>Flag</th>
          <th class={th}>v2 code</th>
          <th class={th}>v3 code</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          renamed.map(([flag, before, after]) => (
            <tr>
              <td class={td}>{flag}</td>
              <td class={`${td} font-mono text-[13px] text-muted line-through decoration-subtle`}>{before}</td>
              <td class={`${td} font-mono text-[13px] font-medium`}>{after}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>Other changes in v3:</p>
  <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 marker:text-subtle">
    <li>New flag: Sark (<code class={inlineCode}>CQ</code>).</li>
    <li>Names follow Unicode 18.0. For example, Turkey is now Türkiye.</li>
    <li>Images are from OpenMoji 17.</li>
  </ul>
</Section>

<Section id="license" title="License">
  <p class="text-muted">
    Flag data comes from <a class={link} href="https://unicode.org/Public/18.0.0/emoji/">Unicode 18.0</a> and CLDR. Images are from <a class={link} href="https://openmoji.org">OpenMoji</a>. The package and images are licensed under <a class={link} href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>. Made by <a class={link} href={authorUrl}>Risan Bagja Pradana</a>, source on <a class={link} href={repoUrl}>GitHub</a>.
  </p>
</Section>
